# Placeholder mounted at /certs/db-ca.pem when no --db-ca was given.
#
# Never read: without EXTERNAL_DB_CA_FILE the overlay adds no sslrootcert= to
# the database URLs and sets no NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS, so every client trusts its
# own store (sslmode=require). It exists because a compose bind mount needs a
# host path that exists, and `${EXTERNAL_DB_CA_FILE:-./external-db/no-ca.pem}`
# is how one variable drives the whole switch. `bootstrap.sh --db-ca <file>`
# writes the real bundle to db-ca.pem beside this file.
